### 3. An upper bound for the number of sunny lines  

> “Let a configuration … exactly \(k\) of them be sunny. *Each sunny line meets any fixed column in at most one point.* Hence, for any column, at most \(k\) of its points can be covered by sunny lines; the remaining points of that column must be covered by non‑sunny lines.”

